 "note": "AM run. Checked 75 people and filed 13 bullets across 10 people, each verified on its source page by the parent and read back in the Sheet exactly once. Fresh: Charlie Garrelts \u2014 Breeze Airways took over Essential Air Service at Ogdensburg International Airport under a new three-year contract beginning Oct 2026 (ClickNNY, published Nov 2, 2026). A dedicated fresh sweep otherwise found nothing new: items published Oct 22 to Nov 12 across NCPR, North Country Now, NNY360, WWNY and ClickNNY, the four colleges' news and athletics, honors announcements and health-system news named directory members only in already-filed items (Johnston, Walczyk, Evans and Goettl, Tebo) or known-role mentions. Also filed: Corey Delisa's DoorBit Greatest Commercialization Potential prize (filed without a year \u2014 his record says 2024, Clarkson University's own news dates that competition to 2023); Cory Williams's ONNY Holiday Concert production thanks (Dec 2020); Daniel Manor's Seaway Tech Building Trades honor roll (2020-2021, as Daniel Manor III); Daniel Paladin's Ukraine ministry trip with the Network of Related Pastors team (Aug 2024); Ethan Flamand's Spring 2026 Clarkson Presidential Scholar semester; Grace Serene's 2015 solo EP 'Scarlet' and her band's 2021 NPR Tiny Desk Contest submission; Haddon Brown's Chicago School of Violin Making start and first instruments; Haven Fern's 3.98 GPA and President's List record and her student-teaching and first teaching position (2021); and Haydn Demers-St.Hilaire's 2017 pitching win over Hamilton. Not filed: Chidiogor Ofodum's Clarkson blog items are her own first-person writing, so they were not filed as fact; Daniel Paladin's BOB 2025 panel listing rests on a Listen Notes aggregator page only; Gracyn Denny's Hogansburg provider listing rests on an NPI-mirror page for another provider. 8 candidates added to the Research Command ledger (identity holds for Emma Morse, Hannah Hughes, Emily Ramer, Colleen Hackett and Ethan Flamand;